  "text": "To find the value of $\\frac{1}{m}$, where $m$ is the smallest number in the set $\\{a_1, a_2, \\ldots , a_{2023}\\}$, based on the given conditions $\\sum_{i=1}^{2023} a_i = 2023$ and $\\sum_{i=1}^{2023} a_i^3 = 40401$, we can use the Power Mean Inequality. This inequality states that for any positive real numbers $a_1, a_2, \\ldots , a_n$ and for any real numbers $p, q$, if $p > q$, then:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^p \\right)^{1/p} \\geq \\left( \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^q \\right)^{1/q}\n\\]\n\nIn this problem, we have $p=1$ and $q=3$, and since $3 > 1$, we can apply the Power Mean Inequality:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{1}{2023} \\sum_{i=1}^{2023} a_i^3 \\right)^{1/3} \\geq \\left( \\frac{1}{2023} \\sum_{i=1}^{2023} a_i \\right)^{1/1}\n\\]\n\nGiven that $\\sum_{i=1}^{2023} a_i^3 = 40401$ and $\\sum_{i=1}^{2023} a_i = 2023$, we substitute these values into the inequality:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{40401}{2023} \\right)^{1/3} \\geq \\left( \\frac{2023}{2023} \\right)^{1/1}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n\n\\[\n\\left( 20 \\right)^{1/3} \\geq 1\n\\]\n\nSince $20 \\geq 1$ and taking the cube root does not change the inequality, it follows that:\n\n\\[\n20^{1/3} \\geq 1\n\\]\n\nNow, since $m$ is the smallest number in the set $\\{a_1, a_2, \\ldots , a_{2023}\\}$ and the average of the $a_i$s is $2023/2023 = 1$, we deduce that $m \\leq 1$. However, because we have used the Power Mean Inequality, and since $20^{1/3} \\geq 1$, the only number that can satisfy both conditions and the inequality is $m = 1$. This means the smallest number is $1$, and therefore $\\frac{1}{m} = 1$.",
